/*pàgines de l'assistent*/
gps_assistent_0, 				"This application generates a MiramMon Map that you can display in real time.\n\nEnter the map name or accept the default name (GPSMM_aaaammdd_hhmmss).\n\nIf that map exists, it will be updated."

gps_assistent_1_1,				"Turn on the GPS and plug it into the serial port of the computer. Make sure the GPS is set as:\n\t\t- Transmission protocol: NMEA 0183 2.0\n\t\t- Transmission speed: 4800."
gps_assistent_1_2,				"The serial port number %hd has been configured with a transmission speed %ld.\nTransmission speeds of GPS and serial port must be equal. Change this setting if necessary."
gps_assistent_1_3,				"If you have GPS turned on and connected to your computer, you can do a test transmission."
gps_assistent_1_4,				"Transmission test"
gps_assistent_1_5,				"Wait..."

gps_assistent_2_1,				"The cartographic reference systems are:\n\n\tInput: %s\n\tOutput: %s\n\nChange them if it's necessary.\n\n"
gps_assistent_2_2,				"We strongly recommend configuring the GPS cartographic reference system to latitude-longitude WGS84 and make a transformation at your cartographic reference system of choice, if any, from this application."

gps_assistent_3_1,				"You can set the interval of time in seconds that the application reads a GPS coordinate and generates a new segment on the route.\n\nIf you set a short capture time (a few seconds), it will generate a very detailed route."
gps_assistent_3_2,				"You can also specify the interval of time in which MiraMon will automatically refresh the map screen. Note that the refresh time of MiraMon must not be less than the capture time."
gps_assistent_3_segons,			"seconds"
gps_assistent_3_3,				"Refresh time in MiraMon"

gps_assistent_4_1,				"Output map"
gps_assistent_4_2,				"Input\\Output reference system: %s \\ %s."
gps_assistent_missatge_final,	"Click finish and, in the next window, the button 'Capture'."

T_endavant,					"Next"
T_enrere,					"Back"
